IoTHubby is an independent, clean-room implementation of the device/module side
of the Azure IoT Hub and Azure IoT Edge MQTT protocol for the .NET platform. It
does not include or derive from the source code of the Azure IoT SDKs; it
interoperates with Azure IoT Hub and IoT Edge by implementing the same publicly
documented MQTT topic/message conventions. The existing azure-iot-sdk-csharp is
referenced only as a wire/byte-compatibility reference, not for its API or code.

